  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Community Resilience to Climate Risks and Vulnerabilities (BCRC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project &quot;Building Community Resilience to Climate Risks and Vulnerabilities (BCRC)&quot;, aims at strengthening adaptive capacities of communities and improve climate resilience in Chandrapur  and Gujara  municipalities, Rautahat District, Madhesh Province, Nepal. The project is planned for 3 years from March 15, 2025 to March 31, 2028 with the grant period covering one year, March 15, 2025, to March 31, 2026. The project focuses to strengthen and enhance climate resilience  in communities by promoting livelihood diversification, community -led adaptation planning and inclusive governance, including some policy works at local level. We would like to support individual families, communities and local stakeholders to build their capacities on resilience and adaptation to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
